      "writtenOn": "2023-12-01T05:45:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I intentionally check only the absence of the SRV record in the additional answers section, this makes it very clear what case this method is testing.\n\nHaving something like\n\n```\nassertEquals(listOf(\n            MdnsTextRecord(serviceName, 0L, true, LONG_TTL, listOf()),\n            MdnsInetAddressRecord(TEST_HOSTNAME, 0L, true, SHORT_TTL, TEST_ADDRESSES[0].address),\n            MdnsInetAddressRecord(TEST_HOSTNAME, 0L, true, SHORT_TTL, TEST_ADDRESSES[1].address),\n            MdnsInetAddressRecord(TEST_HOSTNAME, 0L, true, SHORT_TTL, TEST_ADDRESSES[2].address),\n            MdnsNsecRecord(serviceName, 0L, true, LONG_TTL, serviceName /* nextDomain */,\n                    intArrayOf(TYPE_TXT, TYPE_SRV)),\n            MdnsNsecRecord(TEST_HOSTNAME, 0L, true, SHORT_TTL, TEST_HOSTNAME /* nextDomain */,\n                    intArrayOf(TYPE_A, TYPE_AAAA)),\n        ), reply.additionalAnswers)\n```\n\nwould make it harder for readers to realize the expectation of this test case - they can spend sometime to find out that the `MdnsServiceRecord` is missing from the expected record list.\n\nOn the other hand, SRV, TXT and A, AAAA records being added to additional answer record for PTR question has already been verified by other test cases, so there may be no necessary to check then again here.\n\nFeel free to unresolve if you feel strong on this.",
